Problem and solution
Target Audience
Frontend developers, UI/UX designers, and software engineers collaborating during whiteboard or napkin brainstorming sessions.

The Problem
Frontend developers waste 30+ minutes manually slicing paper wireframes and napkin sketches into layout boilerplate, flexboxes, CSS grids, and Tailwind utility classes.

Input → Output Workflow
Input: Hand-drawn wireframe sketch/photo uploaded via drag-and-drop or preloaded fail-safe samples, alongside an optional style preset choice (Modern Clean, Dark Cyberpunk, or Minimalist Slate).

Processing: Fast API backend decodes the image via Pillow and sends it to Gemma 4 via the official google-genai SDK using Gemini API cloud endpoints.

Output: Clean, self-contained HTML and Tailwind CSS component markup that renders inside an isolated iframe sandbox in under 3 seconds, complete with a 1-click copyable JSX/HTML code viewer.

Approach and technologies
Frontend: React 18, Vite, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, Lucide Icons.

Backend Service: FastAPI, Uvicorn, Pillow (PIL), python-multipart.

AI Model & SDK: Gemma 4 (gemma-4-26b-a4b-it) via the official google-genai Python SDK on the Gemini API.

Sandboxed Rendering: Isolated iframe using srcDoc with CDN-injected Tailwind CSS ([https://cdn.tailwindcss.com](https://cdn.tailwindcss.com)).

Why Chosen: Using Gemma 4 via the Gemini API provides low-latency multimodal reasoning without local GPU bottlenecks.

Attribution / Credit: Built on top of standard open-source tools (fastapi, vite, tailwindcss, lucide-react).

